{"title":"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(longer)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (longer)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_August_2024)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, August 2024)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b66471dde29ff1899199de380d87c7927420db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2,\\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> be real constants, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> a real variable, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9533ac04d0ae6529faefae8b78bcc83390deee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=\\cos(a_1+x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos(a_2+x)+\\frac{1}{4}\\cos(a_3+x)+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}\\cos(a_n+x).\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"37\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23dbce3f86eb445418bd7fddfc6cce2bf4a98ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1)=f(x_2)=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/9/6e911c8fa903f06dec1e931517a1bd2cddb408e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2-x_1=m\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"10\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269981c02d6475e9e4ac1869e1b063ef377c2847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the period of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c938e3f9dea789595c6290070f7975f45bc4300a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, the period of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f302f4c389b1c58009e2b2653c4c6958f896af6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x_1)=f(x_2)=f(x_1+x_2-x_1)\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />\nWe can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad80e23363a717a96ad99d0e4d1afc5edd1d3ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2-x_1 = 2k\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29ce23c5cf7665dca6fd43c43518d9399c0a956c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in N^*$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/9/6e911c8fa903f06dec1e931517a1bd2cddb408e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2-x_1=m\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"10\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269981c02d6475e9e4ac1869e1b063ef377c2847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28longer.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(longer)\">Solution 2 (longer)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (longer)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the cosine addition formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/267c5d532b2d337e36a14c392e88cc89640c90db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=(\\cos{a_1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos{a_2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\cos{a_3}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}\\cos{a_n})\\cos{x}-(\\sin{a_1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sin{a_2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin{a_3}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}\\sin{a_n})\\sin{x}\\]\" width=\"835\" height=\"37\" />\nThis implies that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb4b23ff831d1695b2a344be2c54f6c3b470b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008a6a6b6bff65823db35ba0106788090db38541.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan{x_1}=\\frac{\\cos{a_1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos{a_2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\cos{a_3}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}\\cos{a_n}}{\\sin{a_1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sin{a_2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin{a_3}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}\\sin{a_n}}\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"47\" />\nSince the period of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593e5c9451474d29ad13abf25283cebf82fd6d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{x}$\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26aa4cc373d7559a315adeaa552e60d44deebbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{x_1}=\\tan{(x_1+\\pi)}=\\tan{(x_1+m\\pi)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"302\" height=\"20\" /> for any natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. That implies that every value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e3437973c6087e4c133a3ba96f1fabacbefa593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+m\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> is a zero of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_August_2024.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_August_2024)\">Remarks (added by pf02, August 2024)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, August 2024)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Both solutions given above are incorrect.\n</p><p>The first solution is hopelessly incorrect.  It states that (and relies on it)\nif <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/aced818899589d02392e6263cd9306af20fad399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1) = f(x_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/39698c11e14ef47fe31dfa1316f59791961a5f9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 - x_1 = m\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"10\" /> for\nsome integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.  This is plainly wrong (think of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea3769858cd70145c7388ce4035f6a9584af65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\pi/3} = \\sin{2\\pi/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />).\nThere is an obvious \"red flag\" as far as solutions go, namely the solution did\nnot use that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de12b6876d947ea3c92b888e7503337bf533b6a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38ec84c8763ada637bdbe067a5abebfc0573762d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_2) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The second solution starts promising, but then it goes on to (incorrectly) prove\nthe converse of the given problem, namely that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de12b6876d947ea3c92b888e7503337bf533b6a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c061c51174596dd1cc12476ffea71e17d534a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1 + m\\pi) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Below, I will give a solution to the problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For simplicity of writing, denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b354a2368b4db5c6233ba8af8151cb4484aeac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = 1/2^{k - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"22\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f847889497fddb42ff04a511ca8240375106a91f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = b_1\\cos{(a_1 + x)} + b_1\\cos{(a_1 + x)} + \\cdots + b_n\\cos{(a_n + x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"481\" height=\"20\" />.\nFirst, we want to prove that it is not the case that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57ccf8d123ba4259e29fba55d9b008874e071492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\nTo prove this, we will prove that the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is at least\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d7217918d4172d0acf673f9544b2cca30692e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = 1/2^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />.  This will ensure that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a206e1278883534274d4761de7fe5300f28ddae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We do this by induction.  The statement is clear for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> has a maximum\nvalue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d7a131edd6f6a49031dbfa7b2a739e91b958f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />.  Assume that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e80c6b6a84ad4015ea436a915435d69edbdd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> terms in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, and the maximum\nvalue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is at lease <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba4f374fefe01c5c78bafbc565a9ab6a6caf289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n - 1} = 1/2^{n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />.  Now add the term\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9156c34c6add57a11e20c3de45c23648417e4c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n\\cos{(a_n + x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" /> (and remember that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d7217918d4172d0acf673f9544b2cca30692e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = 1/2^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />).  This additional term\nhas values in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90d7b3b37e930c42abf0e917c93daaa16a4df824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-1/2^n, 1/2^n]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />, so it can decrease the maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> by\nsubtracting at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34af0ae16e797c69d9e7bd3381dc330590eaac89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> from the previous maximum, which was at least\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff32f207931750f5910253d0ab3d9dc7ddd7d466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2^{n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"21\" />.  So, the new maximum is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34af0ae16e797c69d9e7bd3381dc330590eaac89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now we will the formula\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b2293ce0773d9e028b929970f29739f9aa5b4e8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{(\\alpha + \\beta)} = \\cos{\\alpha}\\cos{\\beta} - \\sin{\\alpha}\\sin{\\beta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"292\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8bdea990cc27db34473c5291340ca8434d9916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = (b_1\\cos{a_1} + b_2\\cos{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\cos{a_n})\\cos{x} - (b_1\\sin{a_1} + b_2\\sin{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\sin{a_n})\\sin{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"744\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a4d94212fa0530c71728f80b061c6cc716406a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1\\sin{a_1} + b_2\\sin{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\sin{a_n} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"308\" height=\"17\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb3afbeeb375831f77309d46f3423c965441d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1\\cos{a_1} + b_2\\cos{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\cos{a_n} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"314\" height=\"17\" /> then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57ccf8d123ba4259e29fba55d9b008874e071492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  So at least one of these sums is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6450fe20e3a83ab6792c53c485674a2b69edf4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\nI will give the proof for the case\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a61964853c60759757d1372412a20f9dc0416f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1\\cos{a_1} + b_2\\cos{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\cos{a_n} \\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"314\" height=\"18\" />.\nThe other case is proven similarly.\n</p><p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de12b6876d947ea3c92b888e7503337bf533b6a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a559ae5330fafc805d49d326d2109e774e8d8d2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_1\\cos{a_1} + b_2\\cos{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\cos{a_n})\\cos{x_1} = (b_1\\sin{a_1} + b_2\\sin{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\sin{a_n})\\sin{x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"701\" height=\"20\" />,\nand similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a4d94212fa0530c71728f80b061c6cc716406a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1\\sin{a_1} + b_2\\sin{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\sin{a_n} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"308\" height=\"17\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09c00e8c0aaaf724125a34648bf4c2535f1db8cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x_1} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347037d523b7301f00729066109a2d23db15355f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x_2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />.  It follows that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> are odd multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/039bf945c704ff98e6f81626bbad32550cc37193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />, so they differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c7913ad7683d80ca363fb9ba6ad07033c340cc2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\pi$\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" /> for some\ninteger <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8c4459634a3d324c72a611e81e9615deeba1d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1\\sin{a_1} + b_2\\sin{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\sin{a_n} \\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"308\" height=\"18\" />, then\nwe can divide by this quantity, and we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ecb019362330e627e44076a13025d29d716ce3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{x_1} = \\tan{x_2} = \\frac{b_1\\cos{a_1} + b_2\\cos{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\cos{a_n}} {b_1\\sin{a_1} + b_2\\sin{a_2} + \\cdots + b_n\\sin{a_n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"428\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Thinking of the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcb09911c740ae4149e7fe2050a9697f44257a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\tan{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> would be enough for many people\nto conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cdf90e8851cad6f3040299d781f888cd295f8d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 - x_2 = m\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.  If we want\nto be more formal, we proceed by writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df44ae86df5574ac7c741a26ba61eb523453268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{x_1} - \\tan{x_2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />.\nSome easy computations yield\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fad07fc9ca8e116a1a85f046e280987bf68ecc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{x_1} - \\tan{x_2} = \\frac{\\sin{(x_1 - x_2)}} {\\cos{x_1}\\cos{x_2}} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"277\" height=\"43\" />.\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/5945521787a250f6c400313e58c4b1643d90a6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(x_1 - x_2)} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />, which implies that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cdf90e8851cad6f3040299d781f888cd295f8d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 - x_2 = m\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, August 2024]\n</p><p>The above solution is great, but why don't we consider another elegant answer relying on geometric sense- \\\\\n</p><p>Consider the following polyline, such that it starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/470a2c607f541814af202217f072918d9d211699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O=A_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> and satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8ce1262ad2824b0861ed35e40375bf3114f55ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{j-1}A_{j}=2^{j-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"117\" height=\"22\" /> and the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c496698e294316fc1ce5c6596d2c09d2d8e33b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{j-1}A_{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> makes with positive direction of x-axis is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192a49d5cbad588f70abf2f2e27cfd536824e83b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, to reach a destination of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/696cf349d1df9bf9becad721e1523013284b343b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n}=A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />.\\\\\nFirst, it is trivial to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/6279d71e0bf7708d4c58d7df7f2aefc47a4cd1c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA&gt;=|OA_{1}|-|OA_{2}|-|OA_{3}|-...=1-1/2-1/4-...=1/2^{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"20\" />, so the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d555a2fb62bf338fd13e9d9ced457fe49932324e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> does not coincide with the origin.\\\\\nSecond, the horizontal coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is just given by the sum of horizontal projection of each segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c496698e294316fc1ce5c6596d2c09d2d8e33b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{j-1}A_{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de0f15ce34f4c31bdb33e15ecc29da76f4153fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(A_{n}=x(A_{n})-x(O)=\\sum_{j=1}^{n}(x(A_{j})-x(A_{j-1}))=\\sum_{j=1}^{n}cos(a_{j})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"477\" height=\"55\" />.\\\\\nMore importantly, when we rotate this polyline with center O and angle x, we can see that each term in the summation above is replaced with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7abc5cf7a9e972cba507b6df00b9cc39ab615e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos(a_{j}+x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />. So f(x) is just the horizontal coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> rotated by angle x.\\\\\nNow the simple observation is that, OA needs to be vertical if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c9cbf3e3c04dc46dea71f60acd0cb704eabc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, and in order to rotate from a vertical position into another one, you must rotate by an integer multiple times of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p><p>[Soultion by KROSA1910, Sep 2025]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO\" title=\"1969 IMO\">1969 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017134117\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 539/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18831/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.662      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    8.662      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16044:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017134117 and revision id 260575. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}